# Vercel builds the React app in web/ and publishes web/dist, and runs the
# credential-free API as one Python serverless function (api/index.py).
#
# The project's Python modules are NOT excluded any more: the function imports
# them, and vercel.json's functions.includeFiles glob bundles them. Excluding
# them was correct when the only backend was Cloud Run; it would now produce a
# function that cannot import its own catalogue.

# The Earth Engine backend belongs on Cloud Run, not in a serverless function —
# earthengine-api and its Google client stack blow past the bundle limit.
# Anchored, all of them. Unanchored these are gitignore patterns matching at
# any depth: a bare `requirements.txt` also excluded api/requirements.txt, so
# Vercel found no Python manifest, installed nothing, and every request died
# with ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'fastapi' — while the modules
# themselves bundled correctly and made it look like an application fault.
/app.py
/ee_series.py
/Dockerfile
/.dockerignore
/requirements.txt
/requirements-dev.txt
/pytest.ini

# Leading slashes are load-bearing. .vercelignore uses .gitignore syntax,
# where a bare `scripts/` matches at ANY depth — it also excluded
# web/scripts/copy-maplibre-worker.mjs, which `prebuild` runs, so the build
# died with MODULE_NOT_FOUND before Vite started.
/bench/
/ingest/
/scripts/
/tests/
/docs/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
venv/
.venv/

# The prototype is kept in the repo for reference but is not deployed.
/site-scanner.html

# demo/ is NOT excluded: vercel.json's buildCommand copies
# demo/site-scanner-demo.html into the build so it is served at /demo.

service-account-key.json
*.key.json
*-[0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f]*.json
**/ee-backend/
.env
.env.*

# Installed and built artefacts. Vercel runs `npm --prefix web ci` and the
# build itself, so uploading either is waste — and node_modules alone is
# ~244 MB, enough to kill the upload with a bare `Error: fetch failed`.
**/node_modules/
web/dist/
.git/
